    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), who both benefit from ideal matchups against high-xERA arms and park factors that significantly elevate their scoring potential. **Lawrence Butler** is our strongest play, leveraging a massive +13% platoon advantage against Tyler Phillips, while **Luis Arraez** leads off against a vulnerable Ryan Feltner, whose 4.97 xERA creates a target-rich environment. Both **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) and **Drew Gilbert** (62.67) also feast on the Feltner matchup, with the favorable park dynamics providing a substantial boost that compensates for their spots in the order. **Jonathan Aranda** (66.98) remains a high-floor play at 1B, capitalizing on an favorable xwOBA metric and a favorable matchup against Spencer Arrighetti to maintain a strong daily efficiency score.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Geraldo Perdomo** (50.71), who narrowly missed the final cut behind **Masyn Winn**. While **Geraldo Perdomo** carries high stolen base utility, the optimizer penalized him for the tough matchup against Kyle Harrison (2.97 xERA), choosing **Masyn Winn** for his relative stability, despite **Masyn Winn** facing the threat of a potential hold-out from opposing pitcher David Peterson. On the risk front, both **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh** are subject to \"Lineup Pending\" volatility; **Cal Raleigh** is a particularly high-risk start (41.14) as he squares off against the elite arm of Dylan Cease. We have safely sidelined the injured **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and the inactive **Bryson Stott**, ensuring we preserve our game caps for the high-efficiency matchups provided by **Dylan Beavers** (66.64) and **Taylor Ward** (57.98) against Brady Singer.",
